{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "meridian/combat-energy",
  "title": "combat.energy/1",
  "description": "DRAFT by Combat for Tools (docs/combat/energy-movesets.md section 4): data/combat/energy/<fighter>.json, one fighter's energy kit inside Game Design's frame (docs/design/energy-overhaul.md E1-E117, the kit sheet section 14). It holds only what E81 leaves to a fighter; every other number is the frame's. Bands enforced here: bolt speed and damage multipliers (E81, 20% and 15%), the lob's arc (36 +- 6 ticks) and charge levels (28 and 48 +- 10%), the beam's levels (30, 54, 84 +- 10%), the beam's damage and length (15% and 25%), its drawn width (x0.4 to x1.6) and hit width (x0.7 to x1.3, section 20), the struggle trait's push (always 1, E96), the beam's sweep (within 20% of the reference's 32 degrees a second), the grab's arrival (24 to 30 ticks) and catch (40), and the templates. Policy: the top level is closed except keys starting with an underscore; each cell is open past its checked keys, since each fighter names his own look. Cross-references for Tools' xref (proposed): lane is a key of data/art/energy-lanes.json lanes, and light.colour is that lane's light_colour; every atom a cell lists is a key of atoms; the file's name is its fighter in lower case; every fighter is a roster id once he is in the roster; each kit differs from every other in at least three of grab look, grab payoff, the lob's level-2 template, the trap template and the beam's trait (section 14)",
